              ],
              "description": "Answers to common questions about our programs, donating and volunteering with CareHaven Foundation.",
              "items": [
                {
                  "question": "What is the main focus of your organization?",
                  "answer": "We support underprivileged children and communities through education, healthcare and essential resources, creating equal opportunities so every child can learn, grow and build a brighter future."
                },
                {
                  "question": "How can I support your cause?",
                  "answer": "You can donate, sponsor a child, volunteer your time or share our work with friends and family. Every contribution, big or small, helps us reach more children and families."
                },
                {
                  "question": "Are my donations tax deductible?",
                  "answer": "Yes. Donations to CareHaven Foundation are eligible for tax benefits as per applicable laws, and you receive an official receipt by email after every donation."
                },
                {
                  "question": "How do you select the communities or children to support?",
                  "answer": "We work with local schools, community leaders and field volunteers to identify the families in greatest need, and review each case so support reaches the children who need it most."
                },
                {
                  "question": "Can I volunteer with your organization?",
                  "answer": "Absolutely. We welcome volunteers for teaching, health camps, food drives and events. Send us your interests and availability using the form below and our team will get in touch."
                }
              ],
              "aside": {
                "title": "Still Have Questions?",
                "text": "Our team is happy to help you choose a cause, set up a monthly donation or plan your first volunteer day.",
